{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d431","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aec3-3561-7712-8605-2d3fb313aa38"},"sequence":2163,"recorded_at":1780531400004321,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"87248923-bb02-4661-85c0-f4531322bb3e","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"87248923-bb02-4661-85c0-f4531322bb3e","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"87248923-bb02-4661-85c0-f4531322bb3e"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aed5-f748-7770-88db-defbd2c25e22"},"task_id":"01a0aed5-f748-7770-88db-defbd2c25e22","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aed5-f748-7770-88db-defbd2c25e22","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/republish_rev1/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-17ootk results — fault-test-local-crash-boundaries (story-final)\n2|\n3|## Outcome\n4|\n5|Ready for review. The Section 13.13 crash/restart outcome gate ships as an\n6|executable conformance harness (`internal/crashgate`) over the landed\n7|`sessckpt` + `matjournal` owners. No product behavior changed; no owner\n8|source touched (mutant targets restored; `git status` shows only the\n9|candidate paths below).\n10|\n11|## Coverage ratios (production call sites in parentheses)\n12|\n13|- AC rows driven: **4 of 4** (`sessckpt.Store.Capture`,\n14|  `matjournal.Store.Create`/updates/`matjournal.Store.Recover`).\n15|- Reachable boundary paths driven: **48 of 48** (31 of 94 IDs), each with a\n16|  crash, a clean restart, exactly one outcome, and a complete conformance\n17|  record. 72 table rows + 2 real-SIGKILL rows.\n18|- NOT APPLICABLE paths recorded with exact owners, none driven: **121 of\n19|  121** (63 of 94 IDs).\n20|- Section 13.13 clauses discharged in the registry: **9 of 11** (`partial`);\n21|  `13.13#4/#5` journal-halves only, disclosed in the binding gap.\n22|- Section 13.12 rows driven: **7 of 19** (operator interrupt, owner-resume\n23|  lost, rename blocked x2 proofs, disk full x2 proofs, import/open/adopt\n24|  fail before lease x2 probes, adopt fails after lease); the other 12 name\n25|  their unlanded owners in the matrix.\n26|- Rejection cases refused as any successful outcome: **10 of 10** (two live\n27|  authorities, unfenced continuation x2, new-session launch, fresh handle,\n28|  blank relabel, different realm, moved lease x3) — all parked with durable\n29|  blocking evidence, frozen phase, and no second allocation.\n30|- Gating negative tests with narrowing mutants: **9 of 9 KILLED**, each by\n31|  its named behavioral killer; 1 harmless control SURVIVED. The\n32|  token-preserving registry mutant passes static derivation and fails the\n33|  behavioral suite.\n34|\n35|## What was built\n36|\n37|- `internal/crashgate/registry.go` — classified boundary table (94 IDs,\n38|  per-path drivers/owners/notes) + lookup accessors. Pure data; no I/O.\n39|- `internal/crashgate/*_test.go` — derivation test (ID set parsed from the\n40|  pinned v0.6.0 text, zero hand-typed IDs), 72-row conformance table with\n41|  per-row JSON records, rejections, mutual-exclusion/exhaustiveness,\n42|  Section 13.12 rows, real-SIGKILL seams (unix).\n43|- `internal/crashgate/mutant_harness.py` — 9 narrowing + 1 control; runs\n44|  the behavioral suite per plant.\n45|- `internal/crashgate/TRACEABILITY.md` — clause/boundary/seam matrix.\n46|- Registry: `section:13.13` unevidenced→partial (9/11),\n47|  `section:13.12` unmeasured with harness case, 2 new acceptance cases\n48|  (`crash-gate-journal-conformance`, `crash-gate-checkpoint-conformance`),\n49|  `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` re-pinned to\n50|  `a1b48479025ce73cefdde8771879d6b3cdb93c0e4f1ec4051f4b35b79f357fac`;\n51|  pinned report/CLI-output tests and README figures/coverage refreshed.\n52|- README package section; LOGBOOK entry (newest-first).\n53|\n54|## Validation (all exit 0; logs in the evidence tarball)\n55|\n56|| Gate | Command | Result |\n57|| --- | --- | --- |\n58|| tracecheck | `go run ./internal/traceability/